export const CONTRACT_QUESTION = 'Backtest a government-contract-award-only strategy for LMT, RTX, NOC, GD, and HII over the past 12 months, then separately over the past month, against SPY. Buy at the first available market open after an award became publicly available, hold for 30 trading days, and use equal position weights. Before calculating, check whether your tools support these rules and whether the historical data covers both periods. Clearly disclose sampling limits, publication delays, missing prices, overlapping positions, and transaction-cost assumptions. Report the number of completed trades, returns versus SPY, drawdown, and uncertainty where supported. Separate calculated findings from untested explanations. If anything cannot be calculated reliably, identify exactly what is missing instead of inventing results or switching strategies.';
export const PRE_NEWS_QUESTION = 'Does trading on publicly available congressional votes, committee markups, bill introductions, or bill passage before they appear in news coverage produce higher returns than SPY?\n\nTest two years and separately one month. Define which companies each action affects before examining returns. Enter trades only after the legislative information became publicly accessible, allowing for processing time and trading costs.\n\nVerify public-release and news timestamps. Distinguish “before coverage in the available news archive” from “before any news anywhere.” Report missing data and uncertainty. Do not substitute politicians’ personal stock trades.';
